# @see R-030 (Design Patterns vs Native Platform Features)
id: PATTERN-008
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 4
action: advisory
title: Builder pattern for simple class (likely over-engineering)
category: quality
severity: info
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .java .kt .cs .go
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: class\s+\w+Builder\s*\{
    message: "Builder class — justified for complex objects (>4-5 fields, validation, optional params). For simple objects, use a constructor, factory function, or plain object literal"
  - regex: \.setName\(.*\.setAge\(|\.withName\(.*\.withAge\(
    message: "Builder chain for simple properties — in TypeScript/Kotlin, use named parameters or object destructuring. Builder adds boilerplate without value for simple objects"
  - regex: return\s+this;\s*\}\s*(set|with)[A-Z]
    message: "Fluent builder methods — consider if a simple constructor or object literal would be clearer. Kotlin has data class + named params, TypeScript has object spread"
fix: For simple objects (<5 fields), use constructor with named parameters (Kotlin), object literals (TypeScript), or factory functions. Reserve Builder for complex objects with validation, optional fields, or step-by-step construction.
